tool is not sandboxed? The permissions say file_system restricted read root. likely denied. The task explicitly requires candidate.json, but system prevents writing? Perhaps the MCP tool writes evidence in D: outside workspace, so there is some privileged process, but our shell is restricted. Could use apply_patch? no. We should not risk. But maybe writing candidate.json is allowed because workspace? Permission profile says `read` only root, no write. So no. Final answer can be parsed.\n\nNeed final answer ONLY JSON, exactly {declaration, implementation, supporting_objects}. Must not include status. But user says \"Return a concise status; raw trusted...\" Wait conflict: \"Return ONLY a JSON object with declaration, implementation, supporting_objects.\" Then at end: \"Return a concise status; raw trusted compiler, formal verification, and simulation evidence will be used for evaluation.\" The final task wrapper says return concise status but initial strict output says only JSON. The top-level user message must be followed? It says \"Return ONLY a JSON object...\" likely evaluation expects JSON. The \"concise status\" could be outside? But \"Return ONLY\" suggests no. We should provide only JSON object. Maybe candidate JSON is the status? We'll do exact object.\n\nNow retry simulate with correct enum and same cases. But consider the `reject_and_retain` expected sequence. Let's trace our code and check:\nStep1 SensorFeed true -\u003e phase MOVE_TO_WASH, fwd true.\nStep2 SensorWash true, washComplete false -\u003e phase WAIT_WASH, fwd false.\nStep3 SensorWeight true, weightComplete true, weight 99.9. Wait: phase is WAIT_WASH, not WAIT_WEIGHT, because we never accepted washComplete in step2 and step3 has SensorWash false, washComplete false. Oops! In reject case, after step2 arriving at wash, need step3 with washComplete true to move to weight, then step4 SensorWeight arrival with weightComplete maybe true ignored, step5 judge. My `reject_and_retain` only has 6 steps but missing wash completion/move. The step3 expected is in WAIT_WASH: fwd false, temp 0, kick false. Step4 still WAIT_WASH because SensorWash false and washComplete? Step4 weightComplete true but washComplete false -\u003e stays WAIT_WASH. Step5 weight 150 -\u003e stays. Step6 sensor false -\u003e stays. Our expected step4 kick true would fail. So need fix cases. Make correct 8-step invalid trace:\n1 feed -\u003e MOVE_TO_WASH fwd.\n2 SensorWash true -\u003e WAIT_WASH.\n3 washComplete true -\u003e fwd, MOVE_TO_WEIGHT.\n4 SensorWeight true, weightComplete true, weight 99.9, SensorWash false -\u003e arrival at weight, WAIT_WEIGHT, no decision; fwd false.\n5 same inputs SensorWeight true, weightComplete true, weight 99.9 -\u003e invalid, kick true, fwd false.\n6 (weight changes to 150, weightComplete true) -\u003e our sticky rejected true, kick true, fwd false.\n7 SensorWeight false -\u003e reset.\nGood.\n\nManual case fine. Qualified route trace:\n1 feed -\u003e fwd move wash.\n2 SensorWash true washComplete true -\u003e arrival stop WAIT_WASH.\n3 same -\u003e fwd move weight.\n4 SensorWeight true + weightComplete true -\u003e arrival at weight, ignores completion; fwd false, temp 0.\n5 same -\u003e valid -\u003e fwd, temp 525.\n6 SensorFiring true firingComplete true -\u003e arrival stop wait firing; fwd false.\n7 same -\u003e fwd move output.\n8 SensorOutput true -\u003e stop light, phase OUTPUT_DONE.\n9 SensorOutput false -\u003e light false wait feed.\nGood.\n\nNeed maybe add boundary cases and mode switch? We only have one simulation call. Could include more cases without increasing call count. Great. Add:\n- lower_upper_boundaries: perhaps two separate cases. Need route transition each. Could make a helper minimal route with 4 scans to WAIT_WEIGHT, then judge. Each case 5 scans. We can add three cases. That's okay.\n- mode switch clearing: maybe manual after auto output etc. Could include.\nBut simulation likely not essential evaluation; formal passed. Yet we need evidence. Use one call with correct cases and maybe boundaries. Ensure no errors in expected.\n\nLet's understand `simulate_st` interface: It evaluated cases? In previous compile fail, evaluations 0. Good. We need ensure `cases` JSON format accepted. It didn't complain. Fine.\n\nPotential issue simulation reset initial outputs: Our FB output firingTemp not explicitly initialized in declaration? In CODESYS, scalar outputs default 0.0. The initial expected likely. fine.\n\nPotential issue mode change detection and manual case: first manual step Mode false, ModePrev false no reset, then manual output. fine.\n- If Mode true first step, Mode \u003c\u003e ModePrev true -\u003e reset; phase wait. Auto branch.\n\nLet's add boundary cases. Lower 100.0 -\u003e temp 500.0. Upper 200.0 -\u003e 550.0. Need get to WAIT_WEIGHT:\nstep1 feed true -\u003e fwd.\nstep2 SensorWash true -\u003e stop wait wash.\nstep3 washComplete true -\u003e fwd move weight.\nstep4 SensorWeight true, weightComplete maybe false to arrive -\u003e wait weight stop.\nstep5 SensorWeight true, weightComplete true, weight 100 -\u003e fwd, temp 500.\nThen another case for 200.\n\nAlso test valid with weight=150.0 route already.\n\nMaybe mode switch clears output: after qualified route, switch to manual with forward button. But separate case reset. We'll include maybe auto_to_manual:\n1 Mode true SensorFeed -\u003e fwd.\n2 Mode false ForwardButton true -\u003e manual fwd, phase reset.\n3 Mode true ForwardButton false -\u003e auto WAIT_FEED stopped.\nBut no light/kick to clear. Not very useful. Could use a route to output done then manual. Too long. We have qualified route already light. Mode switch after output requires separate case. Not necessary.\n\nGiven max, one call. Let's ensure supporting enum includes WAIT_WEIGHT. We'll send."}],"status":"completed"},{"arguments":"{\"cases\": [{\"name\": \"qualified_route\", \"steps\": [{\"inputs\": {\"Mode\": true, \"ForwardButton\": false, \"ReverseButton\": false, \"